# Rust
target/
**/target/
*.pdb

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# Benchmark artifacts — regenerable, and enormous.
# Generated data is never committed; the generator + seed reproduce it exactly.
bench/data/
bench/results/*.raw
*.tsv
*.tsv.gz

# ...except the IEEE MAC-assignment table, which `crates/uops-oui/data/README.md` has a
# section titled "Why this is committed rather than downloaded" about: an air-gapped build
# cannot fetch it, and `include_str!` needs it present at compile time. The blanket rule
# above was written for bench/ artifacts and caught this one too, so it was never committed
# and three CI jobs — Clippy, the RustCrypto build, and the sqlx metadata check — failed on
# every push with `couldn't read .../data/assignments.tsv`. 1.7 MB, and the document that
# says it is committed was right.
!crates/uops-oui/data/assignments.tsv

# Secrets. Nothing in this project should ever hold key material in the tree,
# but defence in depth costs nothing.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.kek
secrets/

# Local overrides
docker-compose.override.yml
.claude/settings.local.json

# OS / editor
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
target-linux/

# Cookie jars from curl when driving the API by hand. Two have been committed by accident;
# the pattern is cheaper than remembering.
/[a-z].txt

# Python bytecode, from scripts/ being imported rather than run
__pycache__/
*.pyc
